      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-19803",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/45/45b9a58af2bb5defcd68b5d22d528de393ef7b4b27f38830b2b548e9aac82e27.png)\n\nThe base of a solid is the region enclosed by the curve $x = \\sqrt{1 - y^{2}}$ and the $y$-axis from $y = 0$ to $y = 1$, as shown in the picture. Cross-sections perpendicular to the $y$-axis are rectangles. Given that the height of each rectangle is $3$ times the length of its base, calculate the volume of the solid.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
    },
    {
      ":db/id": 17592186101461,
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/type": {
                ":db/ident": ":answer.type/math"
              },
              ":answer/value": "2\\displaystyle \\int_{-1}^{0}(1 + y)dy",
              ":db/id": 17592186099928
            },
            {
              ":answer/type": {
                ":db/ident": ":answer.type/math"
              },
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{1}{2}\\displaystyle \\int_{-1}^{0}\\sqrt{1 + y}dy",
              ":db/id": 17592186099929
            },
            {
              ":answer/type": {
                ":db/ident": ":answer.type/math"
              },
              ":answer/value": "\\displaystyle \\int_{-1}^{0}(1 + 2y + y^{2})^{2}dy",
