      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-50425",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/00/00cfc8e59fdbf6563aec6e2699efcf4f408aca0fad6bcdd2a42701feace58e09.png)\n\nThe base of a solid is the region enclosed by the line $x = y + 1$ and the $y$-axis from $y =-1$ to $y = 0$, as shown in the picture. Cross-sections perpendicular to the $y$-axis are rectangles. If the height of each rectangle is $\\frac{1}{2}$ times the length of its base, which integral gives the volume of the solid?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
